# BUGS

`Tflush` cancels nothing, and the client does not send it: a read a server holds, such as a ping(8) with no reply, waits until it is answered; only a connection that sets a timeout of its own gives up.
Both come with the pipelined client and server.

Before `Tversion` a `Tflush` is answered with an `Rerror`, `fid already in use`, as every request is there; 9P2000 has no `Rerror` for a `Tflush`.
